      {
        "id": "ab4qD_VhNxbQSPDI",
        "content": {
          "type": "Text",
          "format": "html",
          "text": [
            "<h2>Welcome to CLUE!</h2><p>CLUE is a platform that helps your class figure things out together as a community of scientists and engineers. On clue you can work individually and in a group, and you can share your ideas with the class and see other people&#x27;s ideas.</p><p></p><p>In CLUE, everyone works in a group with up to four people. When you start an activity, you can choose a group. You can change groups by clicking on the group number in the upper right corner. Then, you can either join an existing group that has less than four students, or start a new group.</p><p><strong>Right now, make sure you are in the same group as the other students you are sitting and working with. If your groupmates need help, help them! You&#x27;re figuring things out together.</strong></p>"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "Gfa_17RmLPGX_oP7",
        "title": "Text 2",
        "content": {
          "type": "Text",
          "format": "html",
          "text": [
            "<p>Each lesson in CLUE has three parts. The orange tabs above show each part.</p><ul><li>Introduction</li><li>Activities</li><li>Reflection</li></ul><p>When you&#x27;re done with one part, go to the next one.</p>"
          ]
        }
      },
